      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Work-related physical activity (PA), in terms of peak loads and sustained and/or repetitive contractions, presents risk factors for the development of muscular pain and disorders. However, PA as a training tailored to the employee's work exposure, health, and physical capacity offers prevention and rehabilitation. We suggest the concept of \"Intelligent Physical Exercise Training\" relying on evidence-based sports science training principles."},
